1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,211
Chunk-03.

2
00:00:01,211 --> 00:00:11,485
But instead of the diamond ring expected for a fifth anniversary, a black fountain pen rested inside, waiting for me to sign the separation papers that would save his mistress's life.

3
00:00:11,485 --> 00:00:13,226
"Happy Anniversary, Aurora. "

4
00:00:13,226 --> 00:00:14,454
I stared at the pen.

5
00:00:14,454 --> 00:00:18,255
The gold nib glinted under the chandelier lights of Le Bernardin.

6
00:00:18,255 --> 00:00:25,989
Around us, the city's elite dined in hushed tones, unaware that the man sitting across from me was the Underboss of the Bruce Crime Family.

7
00:00:25,989 --> 00:00:28,027
Ethan Bruce didn't look like a monster.

8
00:00:28,027 --> 00:00:29,310
He looked like a king.

9
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:35,905
His tuxedo fit his broad shoulders with military precision, concealing the gun holstered beneath his left arm.

10
00:00:35,905 --> 00:00:41,662
His eyes were the color of burnt whiskey-cold, detached, and utterly void of the love he'd once sworn.

11
00:00:41,662 --> 00:00:44,424
"Sign it, Rory," he said.His voice was low.

12
00:00:44,424 --> 00:00:48,666
It was the same tone he used when ordering a hit on a rival cartel member.

13
00:00:48,666 --> 00:00:50,492
"Ilene is spiraling again.

14
00:00:50,492 --> 00:00:54,322
She threatened to open her wrists if she didn't see proof that we were over. "

15
00:00:54,322 --> 00:00:55,815
I didn't reach for the pen.

16
00:00:55,815 --> 00:00:57,596
Instead, I looked at his hands.

17
00:00:57,596 --> 00:01:04,693
Those large, capable hands that had promised to protect me at the altar were now pushing me into exile for the thirty-eighth time.

18
00:01:04,693 --> 00:01:06,356
This was our twisted ritual.

19
00:01:06,356 --> 00:01:09,635
Ilene Wolf, the Family Ward, would have a manic episode.

20
00:01:09,635 --> 00:01:11,333
She would demand my removal.

21
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:18,027
And Ethan, bound by a twisted debt of honor to her dead father, would banish me to a safe house until she calmed down.

22
00:01:18,027 --> 00:01:20,233
Thirty-eight times I had packed a bag.

23
00:01:20,233 --> 00:01:23,435
Thirty-eight times I had played the obedient Mafia wife.

24
00:01:23,435 --> 00:01:25,351
But tonight was our anniversary.

25
00:01:25,351 --> 00:01:26,930
"Is she here. " I asked.

26
00:01:26,930 --> 00:01:29,177
Ethan didn't flinch."She's in the car.

27
00:01:29,177 --> 00:01:31,619
She needs to see you leave the restaurant alone. "

28
00:01:31,619 --> 00:01:34,445
The humiliation washed over me like ice water.

29
00:01:34,445 --> 00:01:36,675
He had brought her to our anniversary dinner.

30
00:01:36,675 --> 00:01:42,100
He had left her in the limo like a pet waiting to be let out, while he discarded his wife inside.

31
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:43,684
"I am not leaving, Ethan. "

32
00:01:43,684 --> 00:01:46,234
The air around our table dropped ten degrees.

33
00:01:46,234 --> 00:01:47,416
Ethan leaned forward.

34
00:01:47,416 --> 00:01:52,922
The movement was slight, but it radiated the lethal menace that made grown men wet themselves.

35
00:01:52,922 --> 00:01:54,959
"Do not test me tonight, Aurora.

36
00:01:54,959 --> 00:01:56,179
I have had a long week.

37
00:01:56,179 --> 00:02:00,027
I put three bodies in the ground yesterday to keep our borders secure.

38
00:02:00,027 --> 00:02:02,553
I do not have the patience for your defiance. "

39
00:02:02,553 --> 00:02:04,324
He wasn't my husband right now.

40
00:02:04,324 --> 00:02:05,561
He was the Underboss.

41
00:02:05,561 --> 00:02:08,268
And I was just an asset that was malfunctioning.

42
00:02:08,268 --> 00:02:09,473
I picked up the pen.

43
00:02:09,473 --> 00:02:13,678
My hand didn't shake; I had learned to freeze my insides a long time ago.

44
00:02:13,678 --> 00:02:18,905
I signed my name on the linen napkin, not the legal paper."There," I said."A souvenir. "

45
00:02:18,905 --> 00:02:20,282
Ethan's jaw tightened.

46
00:02:20,282 --> 00:02:24,922
Before he could speak, a shadow fell over our table.I looked up.Ilene stood there.

47
00:02:24,922 --> 00:02:26,234
She wasn't in the car.

48
00:02:26,234 --> 00:02:30,480
She was wearing a red dress that was too tight and too loud for this venue.

49
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:33,838
Her eyes were wide, manic, darting between Ethan and me.

50
00:02:33,838 --> 00:02:35,559
"You didn't do it," she whispered.

51
00:02:35,559 --> 00:02:37,003
Ethan stood up fast.

52
00:02:37,003 --> 00:02:38,630
"Ilene, go back to the car. "

53
00:02:38,630 --> 00:02:42,530
She ignored him.She looked at me with pure, unadulterated hatred.

54
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:44,832
"You're still wearing his ring." she shrieked.

55
00:02:44,832 --> 00:02:47,519
The restaurant went silent.Waiters froze.

56
00:02:47,519 --> 00:02:51,118
Ilene grabbed the bowl of lobster bisque from the waiter's tray next to us.

57
00:02:51,118 --> 00:02:52,376
It was steaming hot.

58
00:02:52,376 --> 00:02:55,141
Ethan moved, but he moved toward her, not me.

59
00:02:55,141 --> 00:02:56,672
He reached out to calm her.

60
00:02:56,672 --> 00:02:58,098
Ilene swung her arm.

61
00:02:58,098 --> 00:03:01,009
The thick, orange liquid hit me squarely in the chest.

62
00:03:01,009 --> 00:03:02,626
The heat was instantaneous.

63
00:03:02,626 --> 00:03:06,498
It seared through my silk dress, scalding the skin of my cleavage and neck.

64
00:03:06,498 --> 00:03:09,562
I gasped, the pain stealing the air from my lungs.

65
00:03:09,562 --> 00:03:14,085
I stood up, clawing at the fabric, trying to pull the burning silk away from my skin.

66
00:03:14,085 --> 00:03:15,867
Ethan caught Ilene's wrists.

67
00:03:15,867 --> 00:03:17,811
He didn't look at me.He looked at her.

68
00:03:17,811 --> 00:03:20,829
"Calm down," he soothed."It's okay.I've got you. "

69
00:03:20,829 --> 00:03:25,541
I stood there, dripping with soup, my skin blistering, surrounded by staring strangers.

70
00:03:25,541 --> 00:03:29,706
My husband was hugging the woman who had just assaulted me.Chapter 2

71
00:03:29,706 --> 00:03:32,972
The sharp sting of antiseptic is the scent of my marriage.

72
00:03:32,972 --> 00:03:37,916
I sat on the crinkling paper of the exam table in the private clinic owned by the Family.

73
00:03:37,916 --> 00:03:41,877
My silk dress was cut away, lying in a discarded heap on the floor.
